# What `docker build .` is allowed to see.
#
# This is an ALLOWLIST: deny everything, then name what the build stages actually read. A
# denylist is one new directory away from being wrong again, and the thing it would leak is
# video/.auth/ — a signed-in Chrome profile, which is a live credential. The working tree is
# about 4 GB; the build needs about 20 MB of it.
#
# BuildKit matches each path against every pattern, last match wins, and `!x/**` re-includes
# files whose parent was excluded by `**` — unlike .gitignore, where that does not work.
#
# (.gcloudignore is the same idea for `gcloud run deploy --source`, and .gitignore for git.
# Three files, three readers; none of them reads the others.)

**

# ── Go build (stage: build) ──
# `COPY go.mod go.sum ./` then `COPY . .`
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/**
!internal/**
# The console is embedded by ui/embed.go's //go:embed, so package ui must compile.
!ui/embed.go
# Same again for the guide: internal/app/assistant_guide.go imports package guide, and
# guide/embed.go embeds *.md from its own directory, so the markdown is a build input and not
# documentation here. Without it the Go build fails with "package attesttag/guide is not in std",
# which reads like a module problem and is really this file.
!guide/embed.go
!guide/*.md

# ── Console build (stage: uibuild) ──
# `COPY ui/package.json ui/package-lock.json ./` then `COPY ui/ ./`
!ui/package.json
!ui/package-lock.json
!ui/src/**
!ui/next.config.ts
!ui/tsconfig.json
!ui/postcss.config.mjs
!ui/components.json
!ui/eslint.config.mjs
!ui/next-env.d.ts

# ── Restated after the allowlist, so no future `!x/**` can pull these back in ──
# Secrets and live data first: a signed-in browser profile, real tenant documents, the
# development database, and the dotenv files that hold every key. The `**/` forms matter:
# `!internal/**` above re-includes everything under internal/, and internal/app/.env (a
# test-generated dotenv) would otherwise ride into the build context and `COPY . .`. Root-only
# patterns did not catch it.
video/**
docs/org-*/**
**/.env*
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/bot.log
# Private keys, certs and credential files at any depth.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*credentials*.json
**/*service-account*.json
# The security audits: a map of the product's attack surface. Never in a build layer.
security-review/**
# Big and unnecessary: node_modules, Next.js caches, the local binary, listing screenshots,
# eval fixtures. (The marketing site is not here at all — it is its own repository.)
**/node_modules
**/.next
ui/out
ui/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
/attesttag
assets/**
evals/**
.git/**
**/.DS_Store
